<p>Now once upon a time the King of Astrakhan, at that,<br />
Was sitting on his throne because his throne was where he sat;<br />
And comfortably beside him, and magnificently stocked,<br />
Was a lacquer liquor locker which a liquor lackey locked.</p>
<p>&#8220;My boy,&#8221; the King would often say with granulated voice,<br />
&#8220;I think the 1640 is particularly choice.&#8221;<br />
The boy would understand and so, endeavoring to please,<br />
He&#8217;d try his luck at fitting several likely locker keys.</p>
<p>The King was always miuch annoyed because of this delay:<br />
&#8220;See here, my lad, you&#8217;ve got to throw those other keys away.&#8221;<br />
&#8220;This minute, Sire?&#8221; &#8220;This minute, sir!&#8221; And with a pox that pocked,<br />
He cursed the keys which didn&#8217;t keep his liquor locker locked.</p>
<p>The lackey did as he was bid. Alackalasalack!<br />
He threw them all so far away that no one threw them back.<br />
A silly throw, as I can show, for he was simply shocked<br />
To find he lacked the very one that left the liquor locked.</p>
<p>&#8220;O Sire, I&#8217;ve thrown them all away!&#8221; &#8220;Look here, my liquor lad!&#8221;<br />
&#8220;It so befell I threw as well the one I wish I had.&#8221;<br />
And since it was the kind of lock that isn&#8217;t quickly picked,<br />
The lacquer liquid locker had the little lackey licked.</p>
<p>Unhappy page! In such a rage a king is hard to calm;<br />
A butt or tun of &#8217;51&#8217;s the proper kind of balm.<br />
&#8220;I always liked my liquor locked, from brandy down to beer;<br />
It might as well be lacquer now as liquor under here.&#8221;</p>
<p>Not magic of the magi nor the wisdom of the wise<br />
Could either find the key again or ply where it applies.<br />
The stricken King of Astrakhan soon sickened unto death,<br />
Who tasted not of bitters but what most embittereth.</p>
<p>The little lackey lastly fell into a deep decline,<br />
And evil over all the land to shrivel up the vine:<br />
And now the only vintages of Astrakhan are crocked<br />
In that lacquer liquor locker which a liquor lackey locked.</p>
<p>&#8212; David McCord</p>
